# The Declaration of Consent

[Rubric] *The Celebrant says to the woman*
[Celebrant] *N.*, will you have this man to be your husband; to live together in the covenant of marriage? Will you love him, comfort him, honor and keep him, in sickness and in health; and, forsaking all others, be faithful to him as long as you both shall live?
[Woman] I will.

---

[Rubric] *The Celebrant says to the man*
[Celebrant] *N.*, will you have this woman to be your wife; to live together in the covenant of marriage? Will you love her, comfort her, honor and keep her, in sickness and in health; and, forsaking all others, be faithful to her as long as you both shall live?
[Man] I will.

---

[Rubric] *The Celebrant then addresses the congregation, saying*
[Celebrant] Will all of you witnessing these promises do all in your power to uphold these two persons in their marriage?
[People] **We will.**
[Rubric] *If there is to be a presentation or a giving in marriage, it takes place at this time. See page 437. A hymn, psalm, or anthem may follow.*
